# Wave 6, editor-shell v2a. app.tsx stops being a docked layout and becomes the
# composition root for the islands.
#
# This is the node that actually retires D13's rejected variant: the
# Resizable split and the TopBar above it both leave here, and the inspector
# moves from a docked right-hand panel into the top-left island slot.

file: "packages/editor/src/shell/app.tsx"
doc: "Top-level SPA component: owns the three stores and the adapters, and composes the island frame over the canvas."

constants: [
  { name: "App"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "The layout changes and the bootstrap does not. selectAdapters, the URL\n"
      "param read, loadFrom, seedComponentBindings, startSession, the file\n"
      "sync, the save controller, the editor-theme signal and its persistence\n"
      "all keep their current behaviour.\n"
      "\n"
      "What changes:\n"
      "\n"
      "1. TopBar and the Resizable split are gone. In their place an\n"
      "   IslandFrame whose `canvas` slot is the existing Canvas at full\n"
      "   bleed, and whose six island slots carry Toolbar, Inspector,\n"
      "   FileIsland, ZoomIsland, UndoIsland and StateIsland. Inspector keeps\n"
      "   the props it has today, registerFocus included -- only where it sits\n"
      "   changes.\n"
      "\n"
      "   App branches at the top: StartScreen when no document is loaded,\n"
      "   IslandFrame once one is. StartScreen is rendered INSTEAD of the\n"
      "   frame, never inside it -- the frame is not a page shell, and its\n"
      "   `canvas` slot always holds the real Canvas.\n"
      "\n"
      "2. `onNew` and its 'New diagram' button are DELETED. D11 says there is\n"
      "   no New: an empty diagram has no content to separate from its style,\n"
      "   so the tool has nothing to do with it. The fallback block that held\n"
      "   it becomes StartScreen.\n"
      "\n"
      "3. Load failure stops being a console.error. `loadFrom`'s error branch\n"
      "   sets a signal that reaches StartScreen's `error`, so a bad URL says\n"
      "   so on screen instead of leaving a blank page with the reason in\n"
      "   devtools. A `loading` signal goes with it, set true before the\n"
      "   auto-load fetch and false in BOTH branches, and read by\n"
      "   StartScreen's `loading`. Both signals are new here; without the\n"
      "   second, StartScreen's progress state has no producer and the\n"
      "   slow-fetch case it exists for never renders.\n"
      "\n"
      "4. The islands' onCommand runs runCommand against the context Canvas\n"
      "   hands back through registerCommandContext. App MUST NOT build its\n"
      "   own: three of that context's fields are Canvas-private, and two\n"
      "   contexts would mean two `rect` values, so toolbar zoom and keyboard\n"
      "   zoom would anchor on different points and quietly drift apart.\n"
      "   Hold the accessor in a signal. The islands RENDER immediately and\n"
      "   their onCommand is a no-op while that signal is unset -- do not gate\n"
      "   the slots on it, which would pop all six islands in a frame late and\n"
      "   shift the layout. Do not reason about how many frames it takes; the\n"
      "   no-op is the contract.\n"
      "\n"
      "5. StateIsland's `error` comes from the scene's existing error signal,\n"
      "   which Canvas stops rendering in this same build. Its `mode` is the\n"
      "   active tool's Command.label from the registry when the tool is not\n"
      "   'select', and undefined otherwise -- read the label rather than\n"
      "   writing 'Hand' here, so the island and the toolbar button cannot\n"
      "   call the same tool two things.\n"
      "\n"
      "   Dismissal needs a shell-side signal, because scene.error() is\n"
      "   derived and cannot be cleared by writing to it. App holds a\n"
      "   `dismissedError` and passes `onDismiss` to set it; StateIsland's\n"
      "   `error` is the scene error only while it is not the dismissed one.\n"
      "   RESET IT WHENEVER scene.error() BECOMES A DIFFERENT ERROR -- a\n"
      "   dismissal that sticks across the next, different failure is a silent\n"
      "   loss of the editor's only error surface.\n"
      "\n"
      "6. FileIsland's `fileName` is read from ?file= / ?name= with an\n"
      "   'Untitled' fallback -- exactly what TopBar did. This is parity, not\n"
      "   a fix; see file_island.spec.textproto for why a real document name\n"
      "   needs an adapters change.\n"
      "\n"
      "The theme is still getBundledTheme('blueprint'). Wave 6 also listed\n"
      "'theme loaded like the CLI' for this pillar (§5.7, §8.2's `shell/app`\n"
      "delta) and this spec does NOT do it -- it is not in v2a and not in\n"
      "v2b's scope either. It may simply be obsolete now that themes-blueprint\n"
      "shipped and blueprint IS the bundled default, but that is a call to\n"
      "make and record in implementation-order.md, not to let fall between two\n"
      "specs."
    type: { unsupported: { reason: RAW_EXPRESSION, source_excerpt: "Component<{}>" } }
    uses: ["selectAdapters", "readUrlParams", "createEditorState", "createUiState", "createScene", "createSaveController", "syncToFile", "seedComponentBindings", "findEditorTheme", "applyEditorTheme", "runCommand", "Canvas", "Inspector", "IslandFrame", "Toolbar", "FileIsland", "ZoomIsland", "UndoIsland", "StateIsland", "StartScreen"]
  }
]
